a/leopold-louis-count-palatine-of-veldenz"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/leopold-louis-count-palatine-of-veldenz.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Leopold Louis, Count Palatine of Veldenz</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Leopold Louis was the last Count Palatine of Veldenz, ruling the small principality from 1634 to 1694.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/leopold-sedar-senghor"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/leopold-sedar-senghor.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Léopold Sédar Senghor</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Léopold Sédar Senghor was a Senegalese poet, philosopher and statesman, the first president of Senegal from 1960 to 1980.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/leopold-von-ranke"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/leopold-von-ranke.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Leopold von Ranke</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Leopold von Ranke was a German historian and a founder of modern source-based history.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/leopold-grand-duke-of-baden"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/leopold-grand-duke-of-baden.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Leopold, Grand Duke of Baden</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Leopold was Grand Duke of Baden from 1830 to 1852.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/leopold-prince-of-anhalt-kothen"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/leopold-prince-of-anhalt-kothen.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Leopold, Prince of Anhalt-Köthen</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Leopold, Prince of Anhalt-Köthen from 1704 (ruling in person from 1715) to 1728, was a Calvinist ruler of a small German principality and a keen amateur musician.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/leopoldina"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/leopoldina.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Leopoldina</span><span class="enc-type">Institution</span><span class="enc-snip">The Leopoldina is Germany's national academy of sciences, based in Halle.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/leopoldine-diploma"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/leopoldine-diploma.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Leopoldine Diploma</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Leopoldine Diploma was the charter issued by Emperor Leopold I in 1691 that settled the government of Transylvania under Habsburg rule after the Ottoman retreat.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/leopoldo-batres"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/leopoldo-batres.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Leopoldo Batres</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Leopoldo Batres was a Mexican archaeologist who served as inspector of archaeological monuments under Porfirio Díaz.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/leopoldo-de-medici"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/leopoldo-de-medici.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Leopoldo de' Medici</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Leopoldo de' Medici was a prince of the Tuscan ruling house, brother of Grand Duke Ferdinando II, and a cardinal from 1667.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/leopoldo-galtieri"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/leopoldo-galtieri.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Leopoldo Galtieri</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Leopoldo Galtieri was an Argentine general who headed the military junta as president from December 1981 to June 1982.</span></a></li></ul>
